{"duration_api_ms":62753,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4b7e95a6-2af5-4239-bc89-f1d25d0c2e6f","total_cost_usd":0.461429,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41173,"cache_read_input_tokens":193245,"output_tokens":4667,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1154},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41173,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":647,"cache_read_input_tokens":44693,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2460,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2460},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":14,"outputTokens":4667,"cacheReadInputTokens":193245,"cacheCreationInputTokens":41173,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.461429,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1154,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":8,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The verdict for CAT-02 is **pass**: all five scenarios are proved by their tests. The verdict is written to `tasks/CAT-02/judge.md`.\n\nCAT-02 is an adopted story, so the judge only checks that each mapped test covers its scenario's Given, When and every Then/And, using the scenario's values. Nothing was built, so the ddd, hexagonal, clean-code and dca reviews were not run. I also didn't consult `dca-knowledge`, because checking a test against its scenario involves no pattern decision.\n\n- **Happy path** (browser test, `ProductPageE2ETest`): it clicks \"View Details\" on the \"Domain-Driven Design\" card and checks the product URL, that the product page renders, and the heading text.\n- **Other four scenarios** (integration tests, `ProductDetailPageIntegrationTest`): they cover the image, full description and category; the tab title; the breadcrumb text and both of its links; and the \"Back to Products\" link, followed through to the \"Our Products\" page.\n- **Breaks:** each prepared production change touches only what its own test asserts, and `tests.md` says it turned only that test red. I didn't re-run them.\n\n**One minor finding, which doesn't block:** `ProductCatalogPage.viewProductNamed` (lines 65–73) finds the card by partial text match. \"Domain-Driven Design\" also matches three other seeded books, such as \"Implementing Domain-Driven Design\", and the test then takes the first card. It passes today because the right card comes first. If the catalogue order changes, the test would fail on the heading check; it can't pass on the wrong product. The fix is an exact title match.\n\nTwo things I set aside:\n- The ShopUnderTest, README and Gradle changes in the diff come from the CAT-01 commit `33236c6`, so they aren't reviewed as part of this story.\n- `tasks/CAT-02/build.md` doesn't exist, which fits a story where nothing was built.","ttft_ms":3933,"type":"result","duration_ms":63151,"uuid":"a165b810-2131-4926-9b19-b14d59b9ab92","ttft_stream_ms":2633,"time_to_request_ms":68,"first_content_frame_ms":2633,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
